% ============================================================================
% Personal Master Bibliography (`~/Github/my-bib/reference.bib`)
% Remote: git@github.com:ottercc/bib.git
%
% --- Entry Maintenance Rules ---
% 1. Citekey: <first_author_lastname><4digit_year><first_title_word>
%    - Lowercase ASCII [a-z0-9] only (NO `'`, `:`, spaces). Skip stop words (a/an/the/on/...).
%    - Examples: brown2020language, vaswani2017attention, zhao2023survey
% 2. Title case protection: wrap ONLY acronyms/proper nouns in `{...}`
%    - Good:  title = {Scaling {LLM} Inference over {RDMA} in {GPU} Clusters}
%    - Avoid: title = {{Scaling LLM Inference...}} (locks full sentence case)
% 3. Pages: always use double hyphen `--` (e.g. pages = {123--135}).
% 4. Authors: consistent `First Last and First Last`; space after initials (`Tom B. Brown`);
%    avoid manual `and others` unless huge author lists (let .bst truncate).
% 5. Keep core fields only (drop abstract/keywords/issn/isbn/biburl/bibsource/file/editor/address):
%    - @inproceedings: author, title, booktitle (@string), year, pages (+ optional doi)
%    - @article:       author, title, journal (@string), volume, number, pages, year
%    - @misc (arXiv):  author, title, howpublished = arxiv # "2303.18223", year
% 6. arXiv -> Published: upgrade @misc to @inproceedings/@article IN-PLACE and KEEP the same citekey.
%
% --- Venue Abbreviation Convention ---
% Abbreviate structural nouns only: Proc., Int., Conf., Symp., Trans., J.
% Keep domain words in full + protect acronyms with `{...}`.
%
% --- Emacs Shortcuts ---
%   SPC n b o     -> open this master .bib file
%   SPC l k       -> rekey entry at point to <author><year><titleword> (inside .bib)
%   SPC l c / s   -> clean & align entry / sort .bib buffer
%   SPC n b r     -> refresh citar cache after editing
%   SPC l @       -> insert citation in LaTeX / Org
%   SPC l t b / B -> incrementally sync / prune paper's .bib (via Paper Toolbox)
% ============================================================================

